      "message": "The CMake dependency is there, just not in this file.\n\nsrc/jamidht/CMakeLists.txt does nothing but append paths to the Source_Files__jamidht list (list (APPEND ...)). It declares no target and calls no target_link_libraries, so a dependency cannot be expressed here -- no file under src/*/CMakeLists.txt does.\n\nThe wiring is in the top-level CMakeLists.txt, added by this same patch and present since patch set 1:\n\n  pkg_search_module (yrs REQUIRED IMPORTED_TARGET yrs)   # line 681\n  ...\n        PkgConfig::yrs                                    # line 706\n\nIMPORTED_TARGET carries the include path and the library together, so \u003clibyrs.h\u003e resolves and libyrs links -- the exact counterpart of depyrs in meson. The CMake build of this series is what the gnulinux and macOS jobs run, and it does link libyrs.",
