      "message": "Correct, and fixed. Patch set 1 claimed \"every public method is serialized by an internal mutex\", which takeChanged() does not honour.\n\nThe contract now names the exception instead of glossing over it:\n\n  Thread-safety: every public method that touches the yrs document is\n  serialized by an internal mutex. takeChanged() is the exception: it only\n  reads and clears an atomic flag, so it never blocks and may be called\n  while another thread is inside the document.\n\nDocumenting rather than locking is deliberate: the flag is atomic, the caller polls it from the sync path, and taking the document mutex there would make a cheap poll wait on a merge.",
      "parentUuid": "ce23eec5_2d7251a3",
